article.post
  header.post-header
    p.post-meta
      time(datetime="2026-11-02") November 2, 2026
      |
      | &middot;
      |
      a(href="/authors/sam") Sam Park
      |
      | &middot; 7 min read
    h1 Caching without tears
    p.post-lead
      | Most caching bugs come from one question nobody asked: who is allowed to
      | say that a value is stale? This post walks through three answers.
  nav.toc(aria-label="Contents")
    h2 Contents
    ol
      li: a(href="#ttl") Time to live
      li: a(href="#events") Invalidation by event
      li: a(href="#versions") Versioned keys
  section#ttl
    h2 Time to live
    p
      | The simplest cache forgets everything after a fixed time. It is easy to
      | reason about, and it is #[em always] a little wrong: a value can be stale
      | for up to the full TTL.
    pre: code.language-ts cache.set(key, value, { ttl: 60_000 });
    p
      | Pick the TTL from how long a stale value is #[strong acceptable], not from
      | how long it takes to compute.
  section#events
    h2 Invalidation by event
    p
      | When the writer knows a value changed, it can tell the cache. This keeps
      | entries fresh, but every writer now has to remember to do it.
    aside.callout.callout-warning
      p
        strong Watch out:
        |
        | an invalidation sent before the write commits can be overtaken by a
        | read that caches the old value again.
  section#versions
    h2 Versioned keys
    p
      | Put a version in the key and bump it on every write. Old entries are
      | never read again and fall out on their own.
    figure
      img(src="/img/versioned-keys.svg" alt="Two versions of a key, the older one greyed out" width="640" height="240")
      figcaption Readers only ever look up the current version.
    table
      thead
        tr
          th Approach
          th Fresh
          th Effort for writers
      tbody
        tr
          td Time to live
          td Eventually
          td None
        tr
          td Events
          td Yes
          td Every write
        tr
          td Versioned keys
          td Yes
          td One counter
  footer.post-footer
    p
      | Thanks to #[a(href="/authors/lee") Lee] and #[a(href="/authors/ana") Ana] for
      | reading drafts of this post.
    ul.tags
      li: a(href="/tags/caching") caching
      li: a(href="/tags/architecture") architecture
